{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bi3FrXUU1zgDrDbe5LDhTJ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Voyager 2 Uranus Encounter Summary\n\n**Journey Duration:** \"about 4.5 years\" from Saturn\n\n**Encounter Start Date & Signal Travel:** \"Nov. 4, 1985, when signals took approximately 2.5 hours to reach Earth\"\n\n**Light Levels:** \"400 times less than terrestrial conditions\"\n\n**Closest Approach:** \"17:59 UT Jan. 24, 1986, at a range of about 50,640 miles (81,500 kilometers)\"\n\n**Moons Discovered:** Ten new moons named \"Puck, Portia, Juliet, Cressida, Rosalind, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelia, Ophelia, and Bianca\"\n\n**Naming Tradition Year:** Started in 1787, following \"Shakespeare\" references\n\n**Rings:** \"two new rings in addition to the 'older' nine rings\"\n\n**Magnetic Field:** \"tilted at 55 degrees off-axis and off-center\"\n\n**Wind Speeds:** \"as high as 450 miles per hour (724 kilometers per hour)\"\n\n**Water Ocean Depth:** Evidence suggested \"a boiling ocean of water some 497 miles (800 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\"\n\n**Miranda Flyby Range:** \"only 17,560 miles (28,260 kilometers)\"\n\n**Challenger Date:** \"Jan. 28, 1986\"\n\n**Geometry Note:** The flyby geometry was constrained by \"the possibility of a future encounter with Neptune: Voyager 2 had only 5.5 hours of close study\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b6adecb-ba7a-46bb-9eb3-830f7a6cad57","uuid":"034e8f7c-4b41-4b30-a424-992bbf3132ce","timestamp":"2026-09-26T17:06:32.403Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":327590,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Voyager 2 Uranus Encounter Summary\n\n**Journey Duration:** \"about 4.5 years\" from Saturn\n\n**Encounter Start Date & Signal Travel:** \"Nov. 4, 1985, when signals took approximately 2.5 hours to reach Earth\"\n\n**Light Levels:** \"400 times less than terrestrial conditions\"\n\n**Closest Approach:** \"17:59 UT Jan. 24, 1986, at a range of about 50,640 miles (81,500 kilometers)\"\n\n**Moons Discovered:** Ten new moons named \"Puck, Portia, Juliet, Cressida, Rosalind, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelia, Ophelia, and Bianca\"\n\n**Naming Tradition Year:** Started in 1787, following \"Shakespeare\" references\n\n**Rings:** \"two new rings in addition to the 'older' nine rings\"\n\n**Magnetic Field:** \"tilted at 55 degrees off-axis and off-center\"\n\n**Wind Speeds:** \"as high as 450 miles per hour (724 kilometers per hour)\"\n\n**Water Ocean Depth:** Evidence suggested \"a boiling ocean of water some 497 miles (800 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\"\n\n**Miranda Flyby Range:** \"only 17,560 miles (28,260 kilometers)\"\n\n**Challenger Date:** \"Jan. 28, 1986\"\n\n**Geometry Note:** The flyby geometry was constrained by \"the possibility of a future encounter with Neptune: Voyager 2 had only 5.5 hours of close study\"","durationMs":6345,"url":"<redacted>
